[67.167848, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Write a Python program called quine.py that is a true quine \u2014 it prints its own source code \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mexactly. Then write a second file, polyglot.sh, that is simultaneously valid Python AND valid Bash \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mand prints the same output from both interpreters. Run all files, diff the outputs to prove \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mcorrectness, and print a final summary table showing each file, its language, and PASS/FAIL. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;208m\u25b6 \u001b[39m \u001b[2m\u2234 Thinking #1\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll create both files, run them, verify the outputs, and provide a summary table.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m[Checkpoint cp-1794579290012-1: /tmp/ami-demo-6cTWN6/quine.py]\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;208m\u25bc \u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;35m\u25cf \u001b[39m\u001b[2mRan file_edit(quine.py) +1 -0 0.0s\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;35m\u2713\u001b[39m \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;167mfile_edit\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;243mquine.py\u001b[39m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;35m(+1)\u001b[39m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;35m54 tok\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;243m  \u23bf  diff \u00b7 \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;75mquine.py\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m  \u2502  0  Created new file: /tmp/ami-demo-6cTWN6/quine.py\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m  \u2502  1  Successfully wrote /tmp/ami-demo-6cTWN6/quine.py (new file, 1 lines)\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m  \u2502  2  \u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m  \u